1. (Currently Amended) A method for preparing a cryopreserved acellular dermal matrix comprising:
i) obtaining allograft skin and removing epidermis therefrom;
ii) removing cells from the remaining dermis;
iii) mixing glycerol and a basic solution selected from a buffer solution and an animal cell culture medium;
iv) dissolving sucrose in __the mixed solution from step (iii)__ to a final concentration of 20 to 40% by weight to obtain a cryoprotectant;
v) penetrating the cryoprotectant into the skin from which epidermis and cells in dermis are removed;
vi) freezing the cryoprotectant-penetrated skin in a controlled rate freezer; and
vii) __recovering and packaging the frozen cryopreserved acellular dermal matrix__.

2. (Currently Amended) The method for preparing a cryopreserved acellular dermal matrix according to claim 1, wherein the mixing ratio of glycerol and the basic solution is 0.5 __to__ 3 : 9 based on weight.

3. (Original) The method for preparing a cryopreserved acellular dermal matrix according to claim 1, wherein the buffer solution is selected from PBS (phosphate buffered saline), TBS (Tris-buffered saline) and citric acid buffer.

4. (Currently Amended) The method for preparing a cryopreserved acellular dermal matrix according to claim 1, wherein the animal cell culture medium is selected from MEM (Minimum Essential Media), DMEM (Dulbecco's Modified Eagle Media), RPMI 1640, IMDM (Iscove's Modified Dulbecco's Media), Defined Keratinocyte-SFM __and__ Keratinocyte-SFM __with BPE__, KnockOut D-MEM, AmniomAX-II Complete Medium and AmnioMAX-C100 Complete Medium.

5. (Currently Amended) The method for preparing a cryopreserved acellular dermal matrix according to claim 1, wherein the final concentration of sucrose in the cryoprotectant solution is 30% by weight.

6. (Original) The method for preparing a cryopreserved acellular dermal matrix according to claim 1, wherein the cryoprotectant is penetrated into the separated skin in a 4°C low-temperature bath for 6 to 24 hours.

7. (Original) The method for preparing a cryopreserved acellular dermal matrix according to claim 1, wherein the cryoprotectant-penetrated skin is frozen in a controlled rate freezer at a freezing rate of –1°C per minute.

8. (Currently Amended) An autograft substitute comprising the cryopreserved acellular dermal matrix __having a structure characterized by the absence of epidermis and cellular material in the dermis, and the presence of cryoprotectant penetrated throughout, which is prepared by the method according to any one of claims 1 to 7__.
